# Wiki: Another Stages is canonical

When stage item / recipe / block / GUI / Kube / datapack behavior changes in this mod, **update the Another Stages wiki in the same task** (do not leave docs stale).

## Where

- Canonical docs: `/home/unfamily/git_wiki/Another-Stages.wiki/`  
  (Stage-Items, Stage-Recipes, Stage-Blocks, Stage-Guis, Home, etc.)
- Utils wiki (`Iskandert_Utilities.wiki` Stage-* gating pages): **redirect / short “Moved” notice only** — point to the Another Stages wiki. Do not evolve full stage gating docs there.
- **Stage Actions** stay on Utils/Library — do **not** rewrite them as AS docs.
- Historical Utils Stage pages (link from Home / Moved notices), all of them:
  - https://github.com/unfamily/iskandert_utilities/wiki/Stage-Items
  - https://github.com/unfamily/iskandert_utilities/wiki/Stage-Actions
  - and any other `Stage-*` page under https://github.com/unfamily/iskandert_utilities/wiki
- Do not recreate long stage tutorials under Utils or Library wikis.

## Maniacal explicitness (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

The wiki is for packdevs. **Never** ship a page that is only a code dump + a thin mapping table.

For **every** Kube verb and **every** JSON field on Stage-* pages you must state:

1. **What it does** (runtime effect: craft lock, JEI, drop, close menu, …)
2. **Default** if omitted
3. **Accepted values** / types (ids, tags `#…`, `@mod`, booleans, enums)
4. **How it combines** with other fields (AND / OR / override / ignore)
5. **Side effects** (server vs client, JEI only vs craft, no-owner machines, offline player)
6. **What it does *not* do** when packdevs commonly assume wrong (e.g. `outputs` ≠ whole category; `recipe_types` ≠ serializer id)

Required layout on each Stage-* API page:

- Short “what this system gates” intro
- Full example
- **Method / field reference** — one subsection or table row **per** verb/field with the six points above (not “see JSON”)
- Matcher / stage logic called out explicitly
- Reload commands: what each command reloads
- Supported-mods / coverage where relevant

A bare `| JSON | Kube |` table **without** a “what it does” column is **insufficient**. Prefer:

`| Kube | JSON | Default | What it does |`

If you change a method in Java, update that row in the **same task**. Incomplete wiki = incomplete task.

Do **not** document Unfamiliar Fish / April Fools easter eggs on the wiki.

## Home banner and versions

- Keep **Under construction** at the top of `Home.md` while the AS wiki is incomplete.
- Support table: **26.1.2 = Supported**; **1.21.1 = Not yet (coming)** until that port exists. Do not mark 1.21.1 as Supported prematurely.

## Inheritance and history (do not erase)

Another Stages owns **gating** and **accepted the pre-AS JSON surface** (legacy `iska_utils` / `iska_lib` types still work).

1. **Keep version history** from the old Utils/Library wiki. If a field/feature says it arrived in Utilities `3.5.0.0.0+` or Library `1.12.0.0.0+`, **leave that note**.
2. **Add** the move line: owned by Another Stages when installed; legacy `type` still loads.
3. Do **not** rewrite “Since” tables as if everything started at AS `26.1.2` only.
4. Document new AS-only fields and Kube managers on the AS wiki; mention legacy compatibility briefly where useful.

## Datapack load path

- JSON loads from **any** `data/<namespace>/load/**/*.json` whose root `"type"` matches (`another_stages:stage_*` or legacy item types).
- Subfolders such as `another_stages_items` / `iska_utils_stage_items` are **recommended conventions only**, never a hard requirement in docs or code.
- Prefer bundling many rules in one file (`restrictions` array). See also `json_bundling.mdc`.
- External roots follow Library `bootstrap.datapack_paths` (KubeJS / Open Loader / Global Packs / `datapacks`), including `.zip` packs via `LoadFilesystemBootstrap`.

## Supported mods (recipe lock)

On [Stage-Recipes](Stage-Recipes.md), keep a bottom section **Supported mods (recipe lock)** with mod **id** + **display name** + how (mixin / `RecipeBlockBridge`) + coverage.

- Link to that section from the **top** of the page and again at the **end of KubeJS** and **Datapack** sections.
- **Vanilla (`minecraft`) is always full support** — say so explicitly.
- When a new mod becomes craft/process-lockable, **add a row in the same task**.

## Machines / no owner (recipe lock)

See also `stage_recipe_machines.mdc`. On Stage-Recipes: process machines prevent the recipe from **starting**; **no owner still applies stage locks** (do not imply owner is required for furnace-like gates). Spell that in the method/behavior reference, not only in a footnote.

## What to update when code changes

- New/changed JSON fields, defaults, removed aliases — with history notes above **and** full “what it does” text
- Kube verbs (`AnotherStages.items` / `.recipes` / `.blocks` / `.guis`) — one documented verb each
- Client/JEI presentation (`recipe_viewer`, names, tooltips, textures under `textures/stage_locking/`)
- Reload commands and ownership notes (AS vs Library skip)
- Texture / asset path changes
- Supported-mods table when recipe integrations change

Wiki prose may be Italian or English as existing pages; **code/comments stay English**.
